    metaTitle: 'The Forex Funder Review: $13,400 Payout Complaint', metaDescription: 'The Forex Funder traders allege a $13,400 payout refusal, account lockouts and migration failures. Review the dated complaints and risks.', sourceName: 'Trustpilot', tags: ['The Forex Funder', 'The Forex Funder Review', 'Payout Refusal', 'Trustpilot', 'Prop Firm', 'Account Migration', 'Broker Watch'], isFeatured: true, relatedBrokers: ['the-forex-funder'], linkedSources: [{ label: 'Trustpilot — The Forex Funder reviews', url: 'https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/theforexfunder.com' }],
    content: `<p>The Forex Funder had a 2.5 out of 5 Trustpilot rating, classified as Poor, across 1,574 reviews in the snapshot examined for this article. Recent reviews allege denied payouts, inaccessible accounts and failed migrations. Ratings can change, and customer reviews are allegations rather than adjudicated facts.</p><h2>A Trader Alleges a $13,400 Payout Refusal</h2><p>A reviewer using the name Diogene RW alleged on 5 November 2025 that a $13,400 payout earned during 2024 was refused. Stefan Uys wrote in January 2025 that nearly $3,000 and 23 months of work became inaccessible after what the reviewer described as an acquisition and account migration.</p><p>Brown Lee alleged in December 2024 that login details never arrived for a paid account and refund requests received no answer. These claims concern different transaction stages but share the same practical result: the customer says paid-for access or earned funds were unavailable.</p><h2>Approved Withdrawal Followed by an Alleged Breach</h2><p>Sammy Oyibo alleged on 2 January 2025 that a withdrawal took more than ten days and the account was marked breached after the payout had already been approved. A reviewer using the name Dr Phoze said a challenge passed in February was followed by a two-month wait for a funded account and then another month without payment.</p><p>Two October 2024 reviews describe migration-related lockouts. One reviewer alleged that the new dashboard did not recognize the account email; another said advertised live chat had stopped responding. The Trustpilot snapshot showed no company reply to the cited negative reviews.</p><section aria-labelledby="bestforex-view-heading-179" class="rounded-xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 px-6 py-6 my-8"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">BestForex.io View</p><h2 id="bestforex-view-heading-179" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">Migration does not erase payout obligations</h2><p>Acquisitions and platform changes can cause genuine disruption, but firms remain responsible for account records, access and payment decisions. A prospective customer should ask who legally owes each payout, what happens during migration and which dispute process applies before buying an evaluation.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="about-the-forex-funder-heading-179" class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card px-6 py-6 my-8"><h2 id="about-the-forex-funder-heading-179" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">About The Forex Funder</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm"><div><p class="font-semibold text-foreground">Business type</p><p class="text-muted-foreground">Proprietary trading challenge firm</p></div><div><p class="font-semibold text-foreground">Founded</p><p class="text-muted-foreground">2023, according to supplied material</p></div><div><p class="font-semibold text-foreground">Trustpilot snapshot</p><p class="text-muted-foreground">2.5/5 across 1,574 reviews</p></div><div><p class="font-semibold text-foreground">Primary issue</p><p class="text-muted-foreground">Payout and migration complaints</p></div></div></section><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>What was The Forex Funder&apos;s Trustpilot rating?</h3><p>The reviewed snapshot showed 2.5 out of 5 across 1,574 reviews. Current figures should be checked directly because ratings change.</p><h3>What is the largest payout complaint cited?</h3><p>One trader alleged that a $13,400 payout was refused. This remains a customer allegation.</p><h3>Is The Forex Funder regulated?</h3><p>No financial regulator was identified as overseeing its challenge fees or payout obligations.</p><p>See our <a href="/brokers/the-forex-funder">The Forex Funder profile</a> and compare alternatives in the <a href="/brokers">broker directory</a>.</p>`
