    excerpt: 'The Seychelles FSA says Grand Capital Limited has never been authorised in the jurisdiction, while traders continue to report withdrawal problems.', category: 'news', editorialType: 'Opinion', author: authors[6], publishedAt: '2026-09-07', updatedAt: '2026-09-07', featuredImage: 'https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/2026-09-07_GrandCapital_cover-b1aIE8ClZv0dGxVTeZtJT4t63gqKqM.png', imageAltText: 'Grand Capital was never authorised in Seychelles — BestForex.io Broker Watch', readingTime: '4 min read', wordCount: 472,
    metaTitle: 'Grand Capital Unauthorised: Seychelles FSA Warning', metaDescription: 'Seychelles FSA says Grand Capital was never authorised. Review the live regulator warning, withdrawal complaints and risks before opening an account.', sourceName: 'Seychelles Financial Services Authority', tags: ['Grand Capital', 'Seychelles FSA', 'Unauthorised Broker', 'Scam Alert', 'Withdrawal Complaints', 'Broker Regulation', 'Broker Watch'], isFeatured: true, relatedBrokers: ['grand-capital'], linkedSources: [{ label: 'Seychelles FSA — Grand Capital scam alert', url: 'https://fsaseychelles.sc/media-corner/regulatory-updates/scam-alert-grand-capital-ltd-fraudulent-company-the-fraudulent-company-and-unauthorized-use-of-website-the-unlawful-websites' }],
    content: `<p>The Seychelles Financial Services Authority says Grand Capital Limited, operator of grandcapital.net, is not authorised to conduct brokerage business in Seychelles and has never held that authorisation. The regulator published its warning on 1 July 2024, and the notice remains available.</p><h2>What the Seychelles FSA Warning Says</h2><p>The FSA&apos;s alert states that Grand Capital Limited does not, and at no point has, held its authorisation. It urges the public to investigate providers carefully before sending money or personal information and says the regulator accepts no liability for dealings with the named operator.</p><p>The notice concerns the operator and website identified by the regulator. It is not merely a warning about an unrelated clone using the Grand Capital name. Prospective clients should therefore verify any claimed license directly with the issuing regulator rather than relying on logos or registration numbers displayed in marketing.</p><h2>Withdrawal Complaints Add to the Risk</h2><p>The review material examined by BestForex.io records 13 exposure complaints among 25 recent user comments. One trader alleged that a $500 deposit grew to $800 before repeated withdrawal obstacles appeared in October 2024. Other users alleged that deposits were not credited, trading-volume conditions were imposed before withdrawals and the platform froze during use. These are customer allegations, not findings made by the FSA or a court.</p><section aria-labelledby="bestforex-view-heading-172" class="rounded-xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 px-6 py-6 my-8"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">BestForex.io View</p><h2 id="bestforex-view-heading-172" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">A never-authorised warning is decisive</h2><p>A lapsed license and a regulator saying an entity was never authorised are materially different. A live FSA warning naming the operator should outweigh promotional claims and headline review scores.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="about-grand-capital-heading-172" class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card px-6 py-6 my-8"><h2 id="about-grand-capital-heading-172" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">About Grand Capital</h2><p>Grand Capital offers currency and derivatives trading through grandcapital.net. The Seychelles FSA says Grand Capital Limited has never been authorised in its jurisdiction.</p><dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-5"><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Regulator named</dt><dd>Seychelles FSA</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Warning date</dt><dd>1 July 2024</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Authorisation status</dt><dd>Never authorised by FSA</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Website cited</dt><dd>grandcapital.net</dd></div></dl></section><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Is Grand Capital regulated in Seychelles?</h3><p>No. The Seychelles FSA says Grand Capital Limited has never been authorised to conduct business there.</p><h3>Is the warning about an unrelated clone?</h3><p>No. The regulator&apos;s alert identifies Grand Capital Limited and grandcapital.net.</p><h3>What have traders alleged?</h3><p>Complaint records include allegations of blocked withdrawals, missing deposits and platform freezes. Those allegations have not been adjudicated.</p><p>Compare regulation, costs and protections in our <a href="/brokers">Best Forex Brokers in 2026</a> directory before funding any trading account.</p>`
