    content: `<p>Trustpilot has suspended PipFarm&apos;s headline rating for a guideline breach. Beneath that notice, traders allege overdue payouts, payout-stage account flags and rule changes that reduced their ability to withdraw profit.</p><h2>A $2,000 Payment Reported Overdue</h2><p>Hung Do Tuan alleged on 22 January 2026 that a $2,000 payment due on 5 December 2025 was still unprocessed more than six weeks later. The reviewer said neither PipFarm&apos;s chief executive nor its payments team responded to follow-up messages.</p><p>Govind Mahto alleged on 11 February that a device-identification problem appeared when a payout was requested. Evocati RU alleged on 1 April that permitted leverage and position size were cut from 3% to 1%, followed by a refusal to release profit earned under the earlier terms. These are customer allegations, not regulatory or court findings.</p><h2>Complicated Rules and a Suspended Score</h2><p>One reviewer described PipFarm&apos;s conditions as among the industry&apos;s most complicated, while another said enforcement did not feel transparent. Trustpilot&apos;s intervention does not validate every negative review, but it means the aggregate score should not be used as proof of reliability. The supplied material says 22% of 337 recent reviews were rated one star.</p><section aria-labelledby="bestforex-view-heading-168" class="rounded-xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 px-6 py-6 my-8"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">BestForex.io View</p><h2 id="bestforex-view-heading-168" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">Save every rule before starting</h2><p>Prop-firm rules can change the economic value of an account. Traders should save the terms, payout schedule and account metrics shown when each challenge is purchased.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="about-pipfarm-heading-168" class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card px-6 py-6 my-8"><h2 id="about-pipfarm-heading-168" class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">About PipFarm</h2><p>PipFarm sells evaluation challenges and funded trading accounts to retail traders.</p><dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-5"><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Business model</dt><dd>Prop-firm evaluations</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Trustpilot status</dt><dd>Rating suspended</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Reported overdue payout</dt><dd>$2,000</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold text-foreground">Financial regulation</dt><dd>No regulator identified</dd></div></dl></section><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Why is PipFarm&apos;s Trustpilot rating unavailable?</h3><p>Trustpilot suspended the headline rating for a breach of its review guidelines.</p><h3>How long was the $2,000 payout allegedly overdue?</h3><p>The reviewer said it was due on 5 December 2025 and remained unpaid on 22 January 2026.</p><h3>Is PipFarm regulated?</h3><p>No financial regulator overseeing its evaluation fees or payout obligations was identified.</p><p>Compare account protections in our <a href="/brokers">Best Forex Brokers in 2026</a> directory.</p>`
